<code>sandbox_mode</code>, <code>approval_policy</code>, <code>approvals_reviewer</code>, and
<code>sandbox_workspace_write.writable_roots</code>. Use those settings to decide how much
autonomy the agent gets by default, which directories it can write to, when it
should pause for approval, and who reviews eligible approval requests.</p><p>At a high level, the common sandbox modes are:</p><ul>
<li><code>read-only</code>: The agent can inspect files, but it can’t edit files or run
commands without approval.</li>
<li><code>workspace-write</code>: The agent can read files, edit within the workspace, and run
routine local commands inside that boundary. This is the default low-friction
